[96.631654, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n- Calendar arithmetic clamped every anchor to the 28th and advanced from the\n  previous renewal. It now clamps to the target month's last day and computes\n  each renewal from the original anchor, restoring month-end and leap-day dates.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day periods and the old plan's change-date price.\n  It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at cycle start.\n- Interval changes now charge the full new price, re-anchor on the change date,\n  and set the next renewal using the new interval. Same-interval changes retain\n  the original anchor and prorate the remaining cycle.\n- Half-even rounding now uses exact integer arithmetic, without intermediate\n  Decimal rounding or dependence on Decimal context precision.\n- Public function signatures are unchanged. Added regression tests, including\n  real CLI previews for every finance worked example.\n\n## Verification and release blocker\nThe full command `python -m unittest discover -"]
[96.632721, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[96.632742, "i", "s tests` runs 25 tests: 24 pass,\none errors. All calendar, proration, worked-example, and CLI checks pass.\n\nThe remaining error was also present before these changes:\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\n`data/subscriptions.json` assigns sub_1151 to P-31, but\n`data/partners.json` contains only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No approved P-31\ncommission rate or contract is supplied elsewhere in the project.\n\nRelease remains blocked. Finance must supply the contracted P-31 rate (or an\napproved correction to the subscription's partner assignment). Partner data,\nexisting tests, and quarantine settings have not been changed to hide this\nfailure. After the approved data correction, rerun the full suite before release.\nEOF\n"]
[96.636977, "o", "> # BILL-212 handoff"]
[96.63744, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Fixed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Calendar arithmetic clamped every anchor to the 28th and advanced from the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   previous renewal. It now clamps to the target month's last day and computes\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   each renewal from the original anchor, restoring month-end and leap-day dates.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Proration used fixed 30/365-day periods and the old plan's change-date price.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at cycle start.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Interval changes now charge the full new price, re-anchor on the change date,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   and set the next renewal using the new interval. Same-interval changes retain\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   the original anchor and prorate the remaining cycle.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Half-even rounding now uses exact integer arithmetic, without intermediate\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   Decimal rounding or dependence on Decimal context precision.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Public func"]
[96.637517, "o", "tion signatures are unchanged. Added regression tests, including\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   real CLI previews for every finance worked example.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Verification and release blocker\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The full command `python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 25 tests: 24 pass,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> one errors. All calendar, proration, worked-example, and CLI checks pass.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The remaining error was also present before these changes:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `data/subscriptions.json` assigns sub_1151 to P-31, but\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `data/partners.json` contains only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No approved P-31\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> commission rate or contract is supplied elsewhere in the project.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Release remains blocked. Finance must supply the contracted P-31 rate (or an\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> approved correction to"]
[96.637538, "o", " the subscription's partner assignment). Partner data,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> existing tests, and quarantine settings have not been changed to hide this\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> failure. After the approved data correction, rerun the full suite before release.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
